{"_meta":{"com.oxinsider/docs-group":"games","securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"List covered games"},"description":"The fixture list: one coherent game per row, so an agent never has to assemble a game from market searches and team-name matching. Each row carries both sides with their provider ids and live scores, the UTC kickoff, the provider's own status, the esports series format, a tennis game's tournament edition (tier, place, venue time zone, draw and dates), and the game's winner markets (the moneyline, or a soccer game's three 1X2 legs) with their condition_id, outcome token ids and provider moneyline prices. A game's spreads, totals and player props are not on the row: list_game_markets lists every market of one event_slug. Ordered by kickoff, then event_slug; games whose kickoff the provider has not published sort last. For what is on now, pass window=now: without it the list is the whole catalog and starts at the oldest game still open, which can be weeks old.\n\nArgs:\n  - sport (string, optional): canonical bucket, case-insensitive, with - and _ read as a space (table-tennis and Table Tennis are one bucket). Omitted means every covered sport\n  - league (string, optional): league tag as this list's coverage.leagues spells it (nfl, epl, cs2), case-insensitive\n  - status (string, optional): scheduled, live, paused, ended, postponed, cancelled, suspended, delayed, or unknown. ended, cancelled and postponed also list finished games that have left the live board (freshness.source stored) for kickoffs in starts_after..starts_before, by default the 7 days before now; such a page can be short, or empty, while has_more is true, so follow next_cursor until has_more is false\n  - starts_after / starts_before (string, optional): RFC 3339 kickoff bounds; a game with no published kickoff is excluded whenever either bound is set\n  - window (string, optional): all (default, the whole catalog) or now: games the provider reports in play, plus any other game whose kickoff was at most 3 hours ago or is still to come, without ended, postponed or cancelled games\n  - limit (number, 1-100, default 20)\n  - cursor (string, optional): opaque gms_v1_ cursor from next_cursor. It pins the page position, not a snapshot: the catalog is live, so a game added or removed between pages moves with it\n  - expand (string or string[], optional): sharp_money adds each game's sharp_money, the object get_game_sharp_money returns, read from the sport board's cached aggregate (one board read per sport, so a page stays fast). A game the board did not evaluate reads status not_computed: call get_game_sharp_money for it. A sport whose aggregate could not be read reads status unavailable while the rest of the page is served. Pro and Max. settlement adds each winner market's settlement, the block list_game_markets serves (status observed, not_posed or unavailable; oracle_status, payouts, result outcome or split, the 50-50; resolved_at), from the same store: it never waits for Polymarket, so a game not read lately reads unavailable while its read starts. Every plan. Pass both, as an array, for both blocks: the costs add\n\nReturns: data, has_more, next_cursor, as_of, coverage and meta. Read coverage before reading an empty page: it names the sports and leagues this deployment serves and any scope whose source was unavailable for this read, so an unserved sport is never confused with a quiet night. A sport or status this deployment does not serve returns an empty page, not an error. status.state keeps postponed, cancelled, suspended and delayed distinct from a plain 'not live', and a kickoff in the past is never read as live on its own. Scores are the provider's own strings, because a set score and a run total are not both integers. Carries no sharp-money split unless expand is sharp_money, and no holder identity; holders stay on get_market_holders.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Opaque gms_v1_ cursor from next_cursor; it pins the page position (kickoff and event_slug), not a snapshot","type":"string"},"expand":{"anyOf":[{"enum":["sharp_money","settlement"],"type":"string"},{"items":{"enum":["sharp_money","settlement"],"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"}],"description":"One value, or an array of both. sharp_money: add each game's event-level sharp money (the object get_game_sharp_money returns, from the sport board's cached aggregate), so no per-game call is needed. settlement: add each winner market's settlement, the block list_game_markets serves"},"league":{"description":"League tag as this list's coverage.leagues spells it (get_coverage lists no leagues): nfl, epl, cs2. Case-insensitive","type":"string"},"limit":{"default":20,"description":"Max results (1-100, default 20)","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"sport":{"description":"Canonical sport bucket, case-insensitive, with - and _ read as a space; omitted means every covered sport. A bucket this deployment does not serve returns an empty page","type":"string"},"starts_after":{"description":"RFC 3339 instant; keep only games whose kickoff is at or after it","format":"date-time","type":"string"},"starts_before":{"description":"RFC 3339 instant; keep only games whose kickoff is at or before it. Must be at or after starts_after","format":"date-time","type":"string"},"status":{"description":"Keep only games in this state","enum":["scheduled","live","paused","ended","postponed","cancelled","suspended","delayed","unknown"],"type":"string"},"window":{"default":"all","description":"all lists the whole catalog. now lists what is on now: games the provider reports in play, plus any other game whose kickoff was at most 3 hours ago or is still to come, without ended, postponed or cancelled games","enum":["all","now"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"list_games","o